&lt;div class=&quot;sect2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;_map_reduce&quot;&gt;map reduce&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Convertire una lista di bit in una lista di stringhe e riassumere la lista di stringhe&lt;br&gt;
in una stringa contenente la concatenazione. Come loggare la richiesta inviata(requestBodyContent:byte[])&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-kotlin&quot; data-lang=&quot;kotlin&quot;&gt;log.info(
    requestBodyContent!!.map { it.toInt().toChar().toString() }
        .reduce { request: String, s: String -&amp;gt; request + s }
)&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;_enum_e_classi_sealed&quot;&gt;enum e classi sealed&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;post:&lt;a href=&quot;0038_training_kotlin_enum_sealed_class_post&quot; target=&quot;&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;formazione kotlin enum classe sigillata&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;_functional_interface_e_method_reference&quot;&gt;functional interface e method reference&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;È possibile trasformare un&amp;#8217;entità in un modello di dominio DTO utilizzando un metodo di riferimento (stile funzionale - Java 8)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-kotlin&quot; data-lang=&quot;kotlin&quot;&gt;fun findAllByLoginNot(
        pageable:Pageable,
        login:String)
    :Page&amp;lt;UserDto&amp;gt; {
    return userDao.findAllByLoginNot(
                    pageable,
                    login).map(::fromEntity)
}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;unahttps://stackoverflow.com/a/22245383/837404[buona spiegazione]&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;_catturare_loutput_standard&quot;&gt;Catturare l&amp;#8217;output standard&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-kotlin&quot; data-lang=&quot;kotlin&quot;&gt;package functional

import java.io.ByteArrayOutputStream
import java.io.PrintStream
import java.lang.System.out
import java.lang.System.setOut
import kotlin.test.AfterTest
import kotlin.test.BeforeTest
import kotlin.test.Test
import kotlin.test.assertEquals


class BasicsHOF {
    private val standardOut: PrintStream? = out
    private val outputStreamCaptor = ByteArrayOutputStream()

    @BeforeTest
    fun setUp() = setOut(PrintStream(outputStreamCaptor))

    @AfterTest
    fun tearDown() = setOut(standardOut)

    @Test
    fun `three times dope`() {

        3.times { println(&quot;Hello&quot;) }

        assertEquals(
            buildString {
                repeat(3) { append(&quot;Hello\n&quot;) }
                deleteAt(length - 1)
            }, outputStreamCaptor
                .toString()
                .trim()
        )
    }

    fun Int.times(fn: () -&amp;gt; Unit) = (1..this).forEach { _ -&amp;gt; fn() }
}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;_qual_è_la_differenza_in_kotlin_tra_apply_run_let_also_use_e_with&quot;&gt;Qual è la differenza in Kotlin tra apply, run, let, also, use e with ?&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Confronto delle funzioni Kotlin e utilizzo delle forme lambda Riferimento&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_applica&quot;&gt;applica&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Introduzione Le funzioni Kotlin`apply`, &lt;code&gt;run&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;let&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;also&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;use&lt;/code&gt;, et `with`offrono diversi modi di trattare gli oggetti. Ciascuna ha i propri casi d&amp;#8217;uso e comportamenti. Inoltre, le forme lambda reference consentono di rendere il codice più leggibile e riutilizzabile facendo riferimento a funzioni lambda esistenti.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;La funzione`apply`viene utilizzato per configurare un oggetto durante la sua creazione. Restituisce l&amp;#8217;oggetto su cui viene chiamata.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Esempio con lambda reference:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-kotlin&quot; data-lang=&quot;kotlin&quot;&gt;val someObject = SomeClass().apply(::configureObject)&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Esempio con lambda :&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-kotlin&quot; data-lang=&quot;kotlin&quot;&gt;val someObject = SomeClass().apply {
// configuration des propriétés de someObject
}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_esegui&quot;&gt;esegui&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;La funzione`run`viene utilizzata per eseguire un blocco di codice su un oggetto e restituisce il risultato del blocco di codice.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Esempio con riferimento lambda :&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-kotlin&quot; data-lang=&quot;kotlin&quot;&gt;val result = someObject.run(::someFunction)&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Esempio con lambda :&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-kotlin&quot; data-lang=&quot;kotlin&quot;&gt;val result = someObject.run {
// bloc de code à exécuter sur someObject
// la dernière expression est renvoyée
}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_lascia&quot;&gt;lascia&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;La funzione`let`viene utilizzata per eseguire un blocco di codice su un oggetto e restituisce il risultato del blocco di codice.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Esempio con riferimento lambda :&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-kotlin&quot; data-lang=&quot;kotlin&quot;&gt;val result = someObject.let(::processObject)&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Esempio con lambda :&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-kotlin&quot; data-lang=&quot;kotlin&quot;&gt;val result = someObject.let {
// bloc de code à exécuter sur someObject
// la dernière expression est renvoyée
}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_anche&quot;&gt;anche&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;La funzione`also`viene utilizzata per eseguire un&amp;#8217;azione aggiuntiva su un oggetto e restituisce l&amp;#8217;oggetto su cui viene chiamata&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Esempio con riferimento lambda :&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-kotlin&quot; data-lang=&quot;kotlin&quot;&gt;someObject.also(::performAdditionalAction)&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Esempio con lambda :&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-kotlin&quot; data-lang=&quot;kotlin&quot;&gt;someObject.also {
// action additionnelle sur someObject
}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_logora&quot;&gt;logora&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;La funzione`use`Viene utilizzata per lavorare con le risorse che devono essere chiuse dopo l&amp;#8217;uso. Chiama automaticamente la funzione`close`alla fine del blocco&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Esempio con riferimento lambda :&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-kotlin&quot; data-lang=&quot;kotlin&quot;&gt;someResource.use(::useResource)&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Esempio con lambda :&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-kotlin&quot; data-lang=&quot;kotlin&quot;&gt;someResource.use {
// travailler avec la ressource
}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_con&quot;&gt;con&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;La funzione`with`viene utilizzato per chiamare più metodi su un oggetto senza ripetere il suo nome e restituisce il risultato dell&amp;#8217;ultima espressione.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Esempio con riferimento lambda :&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-kotlin&quot; data-lang=&quot;kotlin&quot;&gt;val result = with(someObject, ::processWithObject)&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Esempio con lambda :&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-kotlin&quot; data-lang=&quot;kotlin&quot;&gt;val result = with(someObject) {
// appeler des méthodes sur someObject
// la dernière expression est renvoyée
}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Utilizzando le forme lambda di riferimento o i blocchi`{}`, puoi incapsulare la logica in funzioni separate, migliorando così la leggibilità e la riutilizzabilità del codice.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_let_function_in_kotlin&quot;&gt;let Function in Kotlin&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Restituisce let l&amp;#8217;oggetto con gli effetti collaterali applicati sopra o nello stato iniziale di ingresso in funzione(let) ?&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;La funzione`let`In Kotlin è utilizzata per eseguire operazioni su un oggetto e restituire un risultato diverso. Tuttavia, è importante notare che la funzione`let`non modifica lo stato iniziale dell&amp;#8217;oggetto su cui viene chiamata&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;table class=&quot;tableblock frame-all grid-all stretch&quot;&gt;
&lt;colgroup&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 50%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 50%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;/colgroup&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Firma&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;inline fun &amp;lt;T, R&amp;gt; T.let(block: (T) &amp;#8594; R): R&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;table class=&quot;tableblock frame-all grid-all stretch&quot;&gt;
&lt;colgroup&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 50%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 50%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;/colgroup&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Uso&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;La funzione`let`è comunemente utilizzata per applicare delle trasformazioni a un oggetto e ottenere un risultato basato su queste trasformazioni.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;table class=&quot;tableblock frame-all grid-all stretch&quot;&gt;
&lt;colgroup&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 50%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 50%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;/colgroup&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Risultato&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Il valore restituito dalla funzione`let`è il risultato dell&amp;#8217;espressione lambda passata come argomento, generalmente il risultato delle operazioni effettuate sull&amp;#8217;oggetto.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;table class=&quot;tableblock frame-all grid-all stretch&quot;&gt;
&lt;colgroup&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 50%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 50%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;/colgroup&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Effetti di bordo&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Sebbene la funzione`let`può avere effetti collaterali sull&amp;#8217;oggetto quando viene utilizzata nell&amp;#8217;espressione lambda, ma non modifica lo stato iniziale dell&amp;#8217;oggetto stesso.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Così, la funzione`let`è un modo elegante per eseguire operazioni su un oggetto ottenendo contemporaneamente un risultato derivato, preservando al contempo l&amp;#8217;integrità dell&amp;#8217;oggetto originale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;toc&quot;&gt;indice&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;olist arabic&quot;&gt;
